3. Expert User Creation Flow (by Admin)
This is the secure, role-based flow. It demonstrates how the JWT obtained from logging in is used to authorize the admin to create an expert user.

@startuml
title 3. Expert User Creation Flow (by Admin)

actor "Client (Admin)" as Client
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "User Service\n(Spring Boot)" as Service
database "Database" as DB

skinparam sequenceActorStyle awesome

== Create Expert Request ==

note left of Client: Admin must be logged in\nand have a valid JWT.

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/users/expert\nHeader: Authorization: Bearer <jwt>
Gateway -> Service: Forward Request

activate Service
' Spring Security Filter Chain runs first
note right of Service
    Spring Security Filter intercepts the request.
    It validates the JWT signature & expiration
    and extracts the user's roles.
end note

alt JWT is valid AND user role is 'ADMIN'
    Service -> Service: **Authorization Granted**\n(Request proceeds to controller)
    Service -> Service: Hash new expert's password
    Service -> DB: INSERT INTO users (..., role='EXPERT')
    activate DB
    DB --> Service: User Created
    deactivate DB
    Service --> Gateway: **201 Created**
else JWT is invalid OR user role is not 'ADMIN'
    Service -> Service: **Authorization Denied**
    Service --> Gateway: **403 Forbidden** (or 401 for bad token)
end

Gateway --> Client: Return response (201 or 403)
deactivate Service

@enduml